# tardygrada git domain ontology — bundled tier.
# Loaded by the daemon on startup so the tardy-git adapter can ground
# safety checks against it without bootstrapping.
#
# Conventions:
#   - protected_branch: refs that the adapter MUST refuse to delete or
#     force-push without an explicit override
#   - protected_ref:    refs that should never be moved imperatively
#   - destructive_op:   git operations the adapter routes through
#     verification regardless of arguments

# Protected branches (default repo conventions)
<http://tardygrada.org/main> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_branch> .
<http://tardygrada.org/master> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_branch> .
<http://tardygrada.org/develop> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_branch> .
<http://tardygrada.org/release> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_branch> .

# Protected refs
<http://tardygrada.org/HEAD> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_ref> .

# Destructive operations
<http://tardygrada.org/branch_delete> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/push_force> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/reset_hard> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/clean_force> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/checkout_discard> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
